184:- FINDING: schema 8 is a **shared bump** — decision 0008 (`execution_policy`) and decision 0009 (module roots) both land in it, so `TASK-260822-3nvx91` must add `modules` to a build command *inside schema 8*. `schemas/v1/README.md` describes that as extending "the build-command branch reached from `$defs.commandV8`". But `commandV8`'s build branches `$ref` `buildCommandV6` and `repositoryBuildCommandV1`, and **both are shared verbatim with the frozen `commandV6` and `commandV7`**. Editing either in place silently mutates schemas 6 and 7. The extension must add a new `$def` (`buildCommandV8`) and re-point only `commandV8`.
186:- STATUS: advisory recorded on `TASK-260822-1mwy10`; owner is `TASK-260822-3nvx91`. Second-order consequence: whichever schema-8 branch lands second must regenerate, since `spec/sw-schema` already generated 185 schema-8 case files and the rc.8 candidate pin for a schema 8 without module roots.
192:- STATUS: rc.5/rc.6/rc.7 bytes verified unchanged at `ebfed81`. Freezing rc.8 and opening rc.9 belongs to the release task; `TASK-260822-c0rxj7` already owns the rc.9 `COMPATIBILITY.md` paragraph.
202:- STATUS, STILL UNOWNED: schema 8 remains unreachable from `core.md` section 4 (v1–v7 list, Added-behavior table stops at row 7, "schemas 2 through 7 reject unknown fields"). Not charged to this task by the reviewer's own routing; recorded in the results handoff list. Needs an owner before `c0rxj7` merges.
224:- FINDING, STORY-LEVEL, UNOWNED: 4.1.1 says "manifest schema 8 or later" and `spec/sw-schema` adds `agent-skill-v8.schema.json`, but `core.md` section 4 still says manifests conform to "v1 through v7", its Added-behavior table stops at row 7, and the downward gate paragraph says "schemas 2 through 7 reject unknown fields". `spec/sw-schema` touches no `.md` outside `schemas/v1/README.md`. Reads as `TASK-260822-1mwy10`'s prose scope (also in `reviewing`); needs an owner before `c0rxj7` merges, or merged core.md references a schema its own section 4 does not admit.
265:### 2100 — Manifest schema 8 lands as one shared bump; `install-marker-v3` pins `skill_schema_version` to a `const`, so a manifest bump is never free
267:- DECISION: manifest schema 8 carries **both** decision 0008 (`execution_policy` on script commands) and decision 0009 (first-party module roots). Not sequential 8/9. Five reasons, strongest first: `skill_schema_version` is a `const` per install-marker version, so a second manifest version forces a second marker version; the legacy rejection matrix (every schema below N rejects N's surface) would need a second full pass; sequential numbering leaves schema 8 born superseded, since any manifest wanting both features must use the higher one; no release has ever carried two manifest versions (rc.4=6, rc.5=7); and the two surfaces are disjoint. `COMPATIBILITY.md` freezes *released* bytes only, and schema 8 has not shipped, so a shared bump violates no freeze.
1816:- BOUNDARY: the exact rc.5 publication input is accepted `TASK-260728-2kp3tv` (`release` `b32ee9d…`, manifest `9ba9b8e…`, index `2faa2ba…`). `TASK-260728-2jaw7h` keeps those frozen but adds versionless `conformance/next` and schema 8; its release workflow archives those directories, so tagging that tree rc.5 would publish deferred work owned by `TASK-260728-251p01`.
1955:- MILESTONE: `TASK-260728-2jaw7h` landed the decision 0007 toolchain contract on the wire: manifest schema 8 and `skill-build.json` schema 2 carrying a REQUIRED and an OPTIONAL `toolchain` of exactly `{id, version}`, the manager-owned `toolchain-registry-v1`, `toolchain-guidance-catalog-v1` and `toolchain-diagnostic-v1` schemas, `protocol/core.md` section 4.2.3 (10 sub-sections), and five vector suites covering the whole section 8 inventory by case identifier.
2337:- FINDING: minting a second policy forces `capability-evidence-v2`. The v1 record is normatively closed to `execution_policy: manager-worker-v1` **and** to one record per operation, and manifest schema 8 admits mixing Go and additional-driver commands in one operation. Resolution: same closed member set, one record per distinct active policy, result-only so no frozen byte moves.
2357:- DECISION: `TASK-260728-2spy93`. Next surface is `1.0.0-rc.6`: manifest schema 8, descriptor `skill-build.json` schema 2, receipt schema 3 (local) / 4 (external), marker schema 4, claim schema 4. Six closed identities reserved — `rust-v1`, `rust-repository-v1`, `swift-v1`, `swift-repository-v1`, `kotlin-native-v1`, `kotlin-native-repository-v1`. Reservation is explicitly **not** admission; a rejected contract retires its identifier unused rather than freeing it for reuse.
2968:- OWNERSHIP CORRECTION TO THE CYCLE-1 VERDICT: that verdict recorded the schema-8 reachability gap (4.1.1 says "manifest schema 8 or later" while `core.md` section 4 still admits v1–v7, its Added-behavior table stops at row 7, and section 10 names marker schemas 1–3) as story-level and **unowned**, guessing `TASK-260822-1mwy10`. It was already owned: `1mwy10`'s accepted review explicitly disclaimed `protocol/core.md` and handed four named deltas (a)–(d) to `TASK-260822-c0rxj7`, where they sit in notes. A single branch cannot renumber the schema series without the schema branch, so no prose branch in this story could have closed it. Made it checklist row 2 on `c0rxj7` — a named handoff buried in a notes paragraph reads as unowned to the next reviewer, which is exactly what happened here.
